---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="GST Compliance, common pitfalls | RDR & Associates"
>
  <section class="relative pt-32 pb-10 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-16 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-20 h-full w-full bg-white"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-50/50 via-white to-white"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#676769_1px,transparent_1px),linear-gradient(to_bottom,#676769_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:4rem_4rem] opacity-[0.03]"></div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#3305d8] mb-6">
        <span>Taxation</span>
        <span class="text-[#676769]/30">&bull;</span>
        <span>January 26, 2026</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-medium tracking-tight text-slate-900 leading-[1.1] mb-8">
        GST Compliance, common pitfalls
      </h1>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-slate-500 font-medium text-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-slate-200 overflow-hidden">
            <svg class="w-full h-full text-slate-400 p-0.5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M24 20.993V24H0v-2.996A14.977 14.977 0 0112.004 15c4.904 0 9.26 2.354 11.996 5.993zM16.002 8.999a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <span>RDR Team</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-slate-300">|</span>
        <span>5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 mb-20 pt-10">
    <div class="aspect-w-16 aspect-h-9 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl shadow-[#3305d8]/10">
      <img src="https://rdrca.com/media/pages/blog/gst-compliance-common-pitfalls/6d5b62266e-1774868231/gst-cover-1200x.png" alt="GST Compliance, common pitfalls" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-32">
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-slate prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:font-medium prose-a:text-[#3305d8] prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline focus:prose-a:underline prose-img:rounded-xl">
      <p>The Goods and Services Tax (GST) has revolutionized the Indian taxation system, bringing uniformity and transparency. However, for many businesses, navigating the complexities of GST compliance remains a challenge. Staying compliant is not just about avoiding penalties; it's about ensuring smooth business operations and maintaining a good reputation.</p><h2>Why Compliance Matters</h2>
      <p>Non-compliance can lead to severe consequences, including hefty fines, interest on delayed payments, and even the suspension of your GST registration. Moreover, a low compliance rating can affect your relationship with vendors and customers who may be wary of dealing with non-compliant entities.</p><h2>Common Pitfalls</h2>
      <p>Here are some of the most common mistakes businesses make regarding GST:</p><figure data-ratio="auto">
        <img src="https://rdrca.com/media/pages/blog/gst-compliance-common-pitfalls/f51b8cfda8-1774868231/gst-pitfalls.png" alt="GST Common Pitfalls Illustration" />
      </figure>
      <h3>1. Incorrect HSN/SAC Codes</h3>
      <p>Classifying goods and services under the wrong HSN (Harmonized System of Nomenclature) or SAC (Services Accounting Code) is a frequent error. This leads to incorrect tax rates being applied, which can result in demand notices from the tax department.</p><h3>2. Mismatched Input Tax Credit (ITC)</h3>
      <p>Claiming ITC that doesn't match the GSTR-2A/2B data is a major red flag. Businesses often claim credit based on their purchase register without verifying if the supplier has uploaded the invoices. This can lead to the reversal of credit along with interest.</p><h3>3. Ignoring Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM)</h3>
      <p>Many businesses overlook their liability under RCM, especially when dealing with unregistered suppliers or specific categories of services like legal fees or goods transport agency services.</p><h3>4. Filing Returns with Mismatched Data</h3>
      <p>Discrepancies between GSTR-1 (outward supplies) and GSTR-3B (summary return) are automated triggers for scrutiny. It is crucial to ensure that the data reported in both returns aligns perfectly.</p><h2>Best Practices</h2>
      <p>To ensure compliance, conducting regular internal audits is essential. Utilizing robust accounting software that checks for errors can also be a game-changer. Furthermore, staying updated with the latest notifications and circulars from the GST Council is mandatory for every finance team.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>GST compliance is an ongoing process that requires diligence and attention to detail. By being aware of these common pitfalls and implementing strong checks and balances, businesses can mitigate risks and focus on growth.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-[#676769]/10 mt-16 pt-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div class="flex gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#676769] py-1">Tags:</span>
        <span class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">GST</span>
        <span class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">Compliance</span>
        <span class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">Tax</span>
        <span class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">Business</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#676769]">Share:</span>
        <a href="#" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-[#3305d8] transition-colors"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-linkedin"><path d="M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z"/><rect width="4" height="12" x="2" y="9"/><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="2"/></svg></a>
        <a href="#" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-[#3305d8] transition-colors"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-twitter"><path d="M22 4s-.7 2.1-2 3.4c1.6 10-9.4 17.3-18 11.6 2.2.1 4.4-.6 6-2C3 15.5.5 9.6 3 5c2.2 2.6 5.6 4.1 9 4-.9-4.2 4-6.6 7-3.8 1.1 0 3-1.2 3-1.2z"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

